   "claims": [
    "General stud spacing for interior walls tends to be around 16 inches on center, while exterior walls may be up to 24 inches on center.",
    "The most common spacing for wall studs is 16 inches on center (16″ OC), which means that the center of each stud is spaced exactly 16 inches apart.",
    "156″ ÷ 16″ = 9.75 Be sure to round up to the nearest whole stud, so in this case, you’ll round up to 10 studs.",
    "Then, add one more stud for the final corner stud, meaning you’ll need 11 studs for this wall.",
    "Note that because center spacing is used, you can use this formula for any width stud, which means that even though a 2×4 does not measure 2″ wide, this formula still works.",
    "You will need two or more Jack studs if you are framing an opening more than 5 feet wide."
   ],
